{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"f4af0fe325eaa40e0fff23ce8b7e9f51ff4bab5de41d0b588e404287835dfa77","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_4252c86e3d6ae76c9688560a32ae72afa4ea33ad27682d83009a5a004c676c5f","overall_assessment":"The paper is well-organized with a logical flow from hardware design space to methodology and experimental validation. The writing is generally clear, and the mathematical definitions for numerical representations are precise. The primary clarity limitation is the absence of a formal algorithmic description (pseudocode) for the proposed search technique, which is described narratively and through figures. Additionally, the caption for Figure 10 is incomplete in the provided text, which may hinder the reader's ability to fully interpret the validation results without relying on the figure's visual content.","paper_id":"BJ_MGwqlg","paper_identity_sha256":"e51cf507697ec6c8971bab7861a48a358d41d571fe65824df00c75246711fa05","prompt_identity_sha256":"adc384689d332fbea16e43314b163106cfe80a7d286c93afcfb4c67ca7416a46","raw_response_sha256":"751d5f8e9edd09d5a70e13685492e915718cd4ee16ab1b5abe68981224dca705","request_identity_sha256":"7ae816d67322b8d4462633204e63013048cb316341e83996d95c42dafd1f719e","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"fedd5f25e43b1e170b327078f258b0f03cc166f93658a042ca5c4888929cbd68","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-031","SRC-032"],"review_text":"The paper is well-structured, moving logically from the hardware design space to the proposed search methodology and experimental results. The terminology is consistent, and key concepts such as 'customized precision' and 'MAC unit' are clearly defined. However, the presentation of the proposed search algorithm (Section 3.3 and 4.4) relies heavily on narrative description and figures rather than a formal algorithmic presentation. While the text explains the steps (e.g., using last-layer activations to predict accuracy, refining with samples), the lack of pseudocode or a step-by-step algorithm block makes it slightly less reproducible for an expert reader. Providing a concise pseudocode block for the search procedure would improve clarity and reproducibility.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-010","SRC-011","SRC-019"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined. The paper clearly defines the encoding for fixed-point and floating-point representations, specifying the variables for mantissa, exponent, and bias. The derivation of the value encoded by a floating-point format is explicit, and the assumption of the leading bit in the mantissa is clearly stated. The use of the 'linear coefficient of determination' as a metric for the search method is introduced clearly in the text. No significant inconsistencies or undefined symbols were found in the mathematical exposition.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-027","SRC-028"],"review_text":"The figure captions are generally descriptive and provide context for the visual data. However, the caption for Figure 10 appears to be truncated in the provided text, ending with 'The model with two evaluated designs produces the same configurations, but requires < 0.6% of the search time.' without a concluding period or full sentence structure, which may leave the reader uncertain about the complete scope of the figure's content. Additionally, the caption for Figure 8 defines abbreviations (FL, FI, M, E, L, R) which is helpful, but the text description of the specific lines in the figure (e.g., 'green line', 'orange line') relies on the reader cross-referencing the visual plot, which is a standard practice but could be slightly improved by explicitly linking the line colors to the specific configurations in the caption or text for better accessibility.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"d71fb9002495d97f510a3ab3b089246c4bf15a2cf200b21fb775435bf4205ae1","paper_id":"BJ_MGwqlg","paper_ordinal":32,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"751d5f8e9edd09d5a70e13685492e915718cd4ee16ab1b5abe68981224dca705","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"BJ_MGwqlg","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"de7828b8911f3745a3b0223c92dbfa6e45dfbd07ac456fda0bbd2949ae1ddb51","request_identity_sha256":"7ae816d67322b8d4462633204e63013048cb316341e83996d95c42dafd1f719e","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":767,"prompt_tokens":16663,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":17430},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"7ae816d67322b8d4462633204e63013048cb316341e83996d95c42dafd1f719e","role":"CLAR","role_ordinal":1,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}